  {
   "@id": "https://doi.org/10.82153/hrpy-t681#quote-c1",
   "@type": "Item",
   "format": "text/plain",
   "content": "diffuse scattering protocols are transferrable between research groups and synchrotron beamlines",
   "isContainedBy": "https://doi.org/10.82153/hrpy-t681",
   "title": "Zielinski et al. 2026, Discussion, paragraph 1"
  },
  {
   "@id": "dew:q1",
   "@type": [
    "dew:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Are 3D diffuse scattering maps reproducible across independent teams, beamlines and visits?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Earlier agreement tests used one group's data from one facility. The diffuse signal is weak and sensitive to beamline, sample handling and processing."
   },
   "creator": "dew:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Zielinski et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/hrpy-t681. Purpose; Introduction, paragraphs 3-5",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.94.12.6180",
    "https://doi.org/10.1063/4.0000087",
    "https://doi.org/10.1107/s2059798324002705"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "dew:q2",
   "@type": [
    "dew:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Do the Mac1 diffuse maps contain features suitable for modeling correlated motion?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Asks whether the maps show halos and cloudy patterns at a quality comparable to earlier lysozyme datasets."
   },
   "creator": "dew:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Zielinski et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/hrpy-t681. Results: 'Separating isotropic and anisotropic contributions'; 'Comparing data quality', last paragraph",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-14933-6",
    "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-36734-3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "dew:q3",
   "@type": [
    "dew:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - How can agreement between two diffuse datasets be judged against their noise?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "A single correlation coefficient over a broad resolution range is dominated by strong features and cannot show where agreement breaks down."
   },
   "creator": "dew:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Zielinski et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/hrpy-t681. Introduction, paragraph 3; Results: 'Comparing data quality and consistency across datasets'",
   "references": [
    "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.94.12.6180",
    "https://doi.org/10.1063/4.0000087"
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "dew:q4",
   "@type": [
    "dew:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - Which experimental variables most limit diffuse data quality and agreement?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Retrospective analysis of less ideal datasets from the optimization process: crystal number, humidity, X-ray dose and crystal size."
   },
   "creator": "dew:creator",
   "bibliographicCitation": "Zielinski et al. 2026, doi:10.82153/hrpy-t681. Introduction, last paragraph; Results: 'Experimental factors leading to high data quality and reproducibility'"
  },
  {
   "@id": "dew:q5",
   "@type": [
    "dew:schema-Question",
    "mira:Question"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "modified": "2026-10-27T00:00:00Z",
   "title": "QUE - How does X-ray dose change the diffuse signal?",
   "description": {
    "@type": "Item",
    "format": "text/plain",
    "content": "Radiation damage is a possible source of correlated disorder, but how it shows up in diffuse scattering was unclear."
   },
   "creator": "dew:creator",
